  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and tranquil weather will prevail through this \nweekend.\n\nClear skies persist across western New York early this afternoon as \na ridge of high pressure across the Midwest into the lower Great \nLakes region slowly drifts eastward. Latest GOES imagery shows a \nstrip of cloud cover moving across Lake Superior along a cold front \nassociated with a surface low up near the Hudson Bay. This weak, dry \ncold front will continue to approach western NY late tonight into \nearly Thursday. Deep layer moisture will be rather limited keeping \nus dry, but a cooling low-level air mass with 850mb temps dropping \nnear 2-5 degC passing over lake temperatures around 60 degF should \nbe sufficient enough lake response for afternoon cloud cover \nThursday southeast of the lakes. Friday will be a few degrees \ncooler, but still seasonable as mid-level heights will begin to\nrise with an upper level ridge building across the central \nCONUS. This will support high pressure building back into the \nnortheast with clear skies and a return to slightly above \nnormal temperatures for late October persisting through the \nweekend.",
